<title>USA: W.R. Berkley Q4 shr $1.12 vs $0.73.</title>
<headline>W.R. Berkley Q4 shr $1.12 vs $0.73.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>					  1996		1995</p>
<p>Gross premium written	   $318,691	  $275,092</p>
<p>Total revenues		     324,414	   284,676</p>
<p>Net income attributable to</p>
<p>   common stockholders	   $21,976	   $14,381</p>
<p>Net income per share		 $1.12		$.73</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding	19,625	    19,554</p>
<p>	  Year</p>
<p>Gross premium written	 $1,262,520	$1,072,590</p>
<p>Total revenues		   1,225,166	 1,021,943</p>
<p>Net income attributable to</p>
<p>   common stockholders	   $76,354	   $49,820</p>
<p>Net income per share		 $3.84	     $2.86</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding	19,861	    17,414</p>
<p>Full company name is W.R. Berkley Corp.</p>
<p>NOTE: Operating income, which company defines as net income before realized investment gains, rose 44 percent to $19.81 million or $1.01 per share for the fourth quarter of 1996, compared ith $13.719 million or $0.70 a share for the corresponding period in 1995. For the year 1996, operating income was $71.52 million or $3.60 per share, from $43.503 million or $2.50 per share recorded in 1995.</p>
